  "simpler_text": "When Tim Costello was in 9th grade, he asked his teacher if poverty was a natural thing, like the tide or the sunrise. He now says it's not natural; it's caused by policies. Costello, now 69, has spent over 30 years fighting poverty in Australia. He has traveled the world, helped in war and disaster zones, was the mayor of St Kilda, wrote books, and is considered a national treasure. People often mix him up with his brother, Peter Costello, who was a former treasurer. Costello is well-known as a Baptist minister and for leading World Vision for 13 years."
